      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Level and momentum: May's $77.6B deficit is a high starting point, but January-April 2026 were tightly grouped at $54.2B, $55.0B, $56.6B, and $54.6B. I treat May as partly persistent because imports rose to $395.3B, but partly temporary because exports fell by $10.5B and nonmonetary gold alone decreased $6.2B in exports."
